<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="S5.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Example reconstructions for a test image, with PSNR to ground truth in brackets. The image is blurred with a <math id="S5.F1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9\times 9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9\times 9</annotation></semantics></math> uniform blur kernel, with subsequent 3% additive Gaussian noise. Observe that PnP-PGD and PnP-DRSdiff have the same eventual PSNR, due to targeting the same underlying functional.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
